<article class="popular-library"><nav class="crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/en/">English home</a> / <a href="/en/library/">Popular library</a></nav><header><p class="kicker">MARTINFIERRO.ORG · THE ENGLISH REFERENCE LIBRARY</p><h1>Argentine Literature: From Gauchesque Poetry to Martín Fierro</h1><p class="intro">Argentine literature reaches far beyond any one poem. But the rise of gauchesque writing offers a revealing way to understand how the nineteenth century imagined the countryside, politics and the power of a speaking voice.</p></header><figure class="hero"><img src="/media/fotografias-v3/biblioteca-critica.webp" alt="Modern editorial reconstruction of a historical literary library" loading="eager"/><figcaption>Editorial reconstruction, not an archival photograph.</figcaption></figure><div class="body"><div class="toc"><strong>In this guide</strong>{sections.map(([h],i)=><a href={`#part-${i+1}`}>{h}</a>)}</div>{sections.map(([h,description],i)=><><section id={`part-${i+1}`}><h2>{h}</h2><p>{description}</p></section>{i===1&&<AdSlot id="article-02-after-start" kind="article"/>}{i===3&&<AdSlot id="article-03-middle" kind="article"/>}{i===5&&<AdSlot id="article-04-late" kind="article"/>}</>)}<section id="sources"><h2>Sources and further reading</h2><p>This original English guide is explanatory scholarship for the general reader. Historical contexts and interpretations should not be confused with the words of the poem itself.</p><ul>{sources.map(s=><li><a href={s.url} target={s.url.startsWith('http')?'_blank':undefined} rel={s.url.startsWith('http')?'noopener noreferrer':undefined}>{s.name}</a></li>)}</ul><p><a href="/en/library/">← Explore the popular library</a> · <a href="/en/characters/">Characters</a></p></section><AdSlot id="article-05-end" kind="article"/></div></article>
